course: dictionary
lesson: 1610
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Cheesy» can mean smelling or tasting of cheese, or silly and too sweet. The words around it give the clue.
explain: Read this: «Pull off a pair of trainers after football and the cheesy smell is a real cousin of cheese.» The words smell and cheese tell you cheesy means smelling like cheese, not silly. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Now look at «a cheesy joke» with no food anywhere. Here cheesy means corny or silly. The clue is the word joke. Different words near a word point to different meanings, so always read the whole sentence.
explain: A «cheesy grin» is a very big, wide smile, often a bit fake, like when you say «cheese» for a photo. Dictionaries list several meanings for a reason, so when you know a word, check whether that meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Cheesy means tasting or smelling of cheese, or full of cheese.
fact: Informal: cheesy means silly, cheap or too sentimental in an embarrassing way, as in «a cheesy song».
fact: A «cheesy grin» is a very big, wide smile, often a bit fake.
fact: In a sentence about feet, cheesy means smelling like cheese: «bacteria eat the sweat and make cheesy smells».
fact: The same word can have several meanings, so check the words around it before you decide.
exercise: «The shop had cheesy pasta with lots of melted cheese.» What does cheesy mean here? | *Full of cheese | Silly and corny | Smiling a fake grin | Cheap and old
exercise: Sam laughed at «a cheesy joke» and groaned. What does cheesy mean here? | Full of cheese | Very fast | Cold and wet | *Silly and corny
exercise: Which word in «the cheesy smell is a real cousin of cheese» is the clue that cheesy means smelling like cheese? | football | *cheese | trainers | pull
test: «She gave a cheesy grin for the camera.» What does cheesy grin mean? | A sad, small frown | A loud song | A grin made of cheese | *A very big, wide smile, often a bit fake
test: Which meaning fits «a cheesy love song»? | Tasting of cheese | Cold and wet | Very quiet and shy | *Too sweet and sentimental in an embarrassing way
exam: Which meaning of cheesy fits «bacteria eat the sweat and make cheesy smells»? | Too sweet in a song | A big, wide smile | *Smelling like cheese, as in the sweaty trainers | Silly and corny
